{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>For a fire has kindled in My nostril.</b> The jealousy kindled and burned a fire in My nostril. Another interpretation: קדחה is as though נקדחה (nif'al form), as in כל אלה חברו, which is as though נתחברו." "<b>And it shall consume earth and its produce.</b> In order to starve them." "<b>And it shall blaze to the foundations of the mountains.</b> What was hidden under the mountains, to flee from the enemies' terror — as the children of Israel did to themselves with the tunnels that are in the mountains. Another interpretation: and it shall blaze to the foundations of the mountains — even in Sheol they will not be able to escape from before the fire."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:09.443782403Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}